e crust. Nate suggested trying this recipe.\n  - frosting: Nate commented that the frosting looked really good and he loves the way it turned out.\n  - something sweet: Joanna expressed interest in trying Nate's sweet recipe, specifically noting she is always up for something sweet.\n  - dairy-free: Joanna likes dairy-free desserts, especially those made with almond milk. Nate previously taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show.\n  - vegan ice cream recipes: Nate taught people vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show last Monday, finding it nerve-wracking but fun, and he learned new recipes.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from her road-trip script, asked about the coolest on-set moment, and commented that her food looked yummy with nice colors and kick.\n  - salt: Salt was used as an ingredient, along with coconut milk, vanilla extract, and sugar, to make ice cream.\n  - new one: Nate asked Joanna about the topic of the \"new one\" after mentioning he baked desserts and made ice cream for a friend.\n  - dairy-free chocolate mousse: Nate likes dairy-free chocolate mousse because it is super creamy and tastes like the real thing.\n  - desserts: Joanna will bring some of her dessert recipes to share with Nate, building on a prior conversation where they discussed dairy-free dessert recipes.\n  - dairy: Joanna is lactose intolerant and requested a dairy-free recipe from Nate.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1986,"context_chars":8016,"retrieval_duration":0.21968412399291992,"response_duration":3.4392597675323486,"total_duration":3.6589438915252686,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions that Nate described the coconut milk ice cream as rich and creamy, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary information to answer the question about Nate's opinion on the coconut milk ice cream he made. It explicitly states that Nate de