anges to live healthier.\n  - Evan: Evan is motivated by adventure on interesting hikes. Last week, he went on a trip to Canada and met an incredible Canadian woman who makes him feel alive.\n  - Evan: Evan congratulated Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach, finding it exciting and rewarding.\n  - family bond: Sam believes it's important to have something that keeps the family bond strong, following Evan's news about his partner being pregnant.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam that his partner was not thrilled but understood an accident involving rose bushes; he plans to be more careful and enjoys small moments outdoors.\n  - Evan: Evan told Sam he is in love with a woman from Canada, whom he married, and expressed joy from viewing a painting that helped him recognize his feelings.\n  - Evan: Evan married his partner last week. Evan was asked by Sam if his spouse is the woman from Canada. Evan had previously mentioned enjoying books, painting, driving, and hiking.\n  - Evan: Evan apologized to his partner for a drunken night and for accidentally damaging rose bushes, promising to be more careful. He is now looking for low-impact exercises.\n  - adventure: Evan asked Sam about his next adventure and mentioned a previous event that turned into a small adventure. Evan's knee injury limits his ability to participate in outdoor adventures.\n  - Evan: Evan is an assistant who supports Sam's new health routine and congratulates Sam on becoming a Weight Watchers coach.\n  - Evan: Evan's son hurt his ankle in a soccer accident last Saturday, requiring doctor visits. He expressed interest in healthy recipes Sam learned in cooking class.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2041,"context_chars":8165,"retrieval_duration":0.35278916358947754,"response_duration":2.307183265686035,"total_duration":2.6599724292755127,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer accurately mentions the 'big family reunion' and specifies the time frame as 'next summer', which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about the family event Evan is planning for next summer. It explicitly states that Evan is planning a 'big family reunion next summer,' which directly matches the golden answer. Additionally, the context includes related details about the reunion, such as the anticipation of family members attending and its purpose, which further supports the completeness of the information provided.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Evan is planning a big family reunion next summer."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_143","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"How did Joanna feel when someone wrote her a letter after reading her blog post?","golden_answer":"Touched","hypothesis":"Joanna felt comforted and appreciated when someone wrote her a letter after reading her blog post. The letter expressed that her story brought comfort to the writer, which likely made Joanna feel good about the impact of her writing. This positive recognition contributed to her feelings of appreciation for her writing efforts.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Someone sent Joanna a letter last week in response to her online blog post. (event_time: 2022-08-07T00:00:00Z)\n  - The letter someone wrote to Joanna was in response to an online blog post she made. (event_time: 2022-08-07T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna's story brought comfort to someone. (event_time: 2022-08-07T00:00:00Z)\n  - Someone stated that Joanna's story brought them comfort. (event_time: 2022-08-07T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna finds moments related to writing to be appreciated because of the positive recognition she is receiving (event_time: 2022-11-04T15:56:00Z)\n  - Joanna feels good knowing that people like her writing. (event_time: 2022-08-22T10:57:00Z)\n  - Joanna created an online blog post about a hard moment in her life. (event_time: 2022-08-07T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna's online blog post concerned a hard moment in her life. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna feels a mix of excitement and terror thinking about her work getting noticed. (event_time: 2022-03-18T18:59:00Z)\n  - Writing helps Joanna express herself in a new way. (event_time: 2022-04-21T19:44:00Z)\n  - Writing gives Joanna a chance to put down all her feelings (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing as a way to express her feelings (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna is inspired to write about self-discovery. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Nate asks Joanna if the letter reminds Joanna of Joanna's childhood. (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:10:00Z)\n  - Joanna engages in writing. (event_time: 2022-01-21T19:31:00Z)\n  - Writing might be a way for Joanna to express creativity. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna perceives the rejection (presumably the rejection letter mentioned previously) as a step back sometimes. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Movies can make Joanna feel many emotions. (event_time: 2022-10-09T10:58:00Z)\n  - Joanna views writing as a huge part of who she is. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - The rejection letter sent to Joanna contained little feedback. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna is proud of finishing the story she wrote. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna enjoys reading in addition to writing. (event_time: 2022-01-21T19:31:00Z)\n  - Joanna is concl