d dialogue she wrote acted out, calling it an amazing and rewarding experience that was the third time this has happened.\n  - supportive group: Joanna joined a writers group described as inspirational, motivating, and supportive, making her feel like she belongs.\n  - people: Joanna shared how rewarding it was to see her written work performed, drawing inspiration from real life and imagination to create characters.\n  - childhood: Nate mentioned a letter that reminded Joanna of her childhood.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - dialogue: Joanna found it rewarding to see the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - thoughts: Joanna uses writing as an escape to express feelings, put down thoughts, and heal, making something good from her thoughts and feelings.\n  - personal experiences and feelings: Joanna shared that meaningful stories arise from vulnerability, exploring personal experiences and feelings, and remaining true to oneself, as acknowledged by Nate.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - loss: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, causing her to feel bummed out. The existing summary mentioned sadness and loss.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - brother: Joanna's brother wrote something that brings back sweet memories, as he used to make her cute notes as a child.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - motivation: Joanna's cork board has inspiring quotes/pictures for motivation and creativity. She gains motivation from having someone to support her.\n  - cute notes: Joanna's brother wrote the cute notes, which reminds her of sweet memories from when they were kids.\n  - moods: Joanna is finding comfort and creativity by tinkering with recipes when in certain moods, which Nate finds satisfying.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - early writings: Joanna's early writings, found in old notebooks last week, include elements of self-discovery that movie producers found interesting.\n  - journal: Joanna uses her journal as her rock while she is busy with writing projects, finding it helps her express feelings and heal.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - writing inspiration: Joanna uses taking breaks and self-care for writing inspiration to maintain inspiration and mental health, seeking balance.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2029,"context_chars":8388,"retrieval_duration":0.1939222812652588,"response_duration":3.327009916305542,"total_duration":3.520932197570801,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer conveys Joanna's feelings of appreciation and comfort, which aligns with the gold answer of h