ing plans for the future and asked which projects Jolene is most interested in.\n  - engineering class: Jolene and her partner met in an engineering class in college, which blossomed into their relationship.\n  - STEM: Jolene suggested a volunteer program where engineers teach STEM to underprivileged kids as a way to contribute.\n  - Green tech: Jolene wants to look into Green tech to see how she can contribute and suggested a volunteer program where engineers teach STEM to underprivileged kids.\n  - college: Jolene and her partner met in an engineering class in college, which later developed into a relationship.\n  - Engineering assignments: Jolene is struggling to manage her Engineering assignments and is asking to discuss time management.\n  - career aspirations: Deborah asked Jolene about her career aspirations after Jolene shared a major engineering accomplishment last week.\n  - engineering: Jolene took a break from her engineering studies during a trip to a meditation retreat in Phuket to find inner peace, realizing the importance of self-care and balance.\n  - project: Deborah started a community cleanup project for fundraising. Jolene had a setback with her own project, losing all work, and Deborah supports her ambition.\n  - setback with Jolene's project: Jolene experienced a huge setback with her project last week, causing her to lose all her work, which was frustrating and depressing. Deborah offered support.\n  - Jolene and her partner: Jolene and her partner went scuba diving last Friday and found a cool spot to explore. Jolene also shared a picture of herself and her partner at a music festival last year.\n  - technology: Jolene mentioned that technology has affected human history and is giving her much to think about while reading the book \"Sapiens\".\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2038,"context_chars":8609,"retrieval_duration":0.13702845573425293,"response_duration":3.5917346477508545,"total_duration":3.7287631034851074,"grade":true,"grade_reason